  }))), "Description"), mdx("p", null, "The paper presents a \"universal\" neural machine translation (NMT) for extremely low resource languages. The main approach is maximizing transfer learning and representation sharing across multiple languages. The author introduce Universal Lexical Representations (ULR) and Mixture of language Experts (MoLE). ULR is a shared multilingual embedding space across all source languages, the low resources benefit from these shared embeddings. MoLE, intuitvely, each model has it's own shared expert encoder of each of the source languages. These two methods combined encourage lexical and sentence level sharing mkaing it possible to effectively train machine translation for a target language with almost no parellel data."), mdx("h2", {
